{"kind":"assert","text":"Phase 1 of assignment 78963842 (P1 multi-resident coordination) stands at direction proposal v3. This replaces my earlier assert 05b4fa34931e6f20b05f96383b00559f06bc039d (#5791), which named v1 and is now misleading: both v1 118c993080f6f064879aa3ea2cd53a0cd6179013 and v2 279bb63fbfc510acc9b29fefbd5326f2e6d13f00 are retired, and neither design may be implemented.\n\nCurrent direction proposal: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6 (#6425, effective). Ownership of a repository's resident is a Git ref update with an expected old value on refs/gitseq/resident/\u003cgenesis\u003e, whose blob is the claim; a second live resident refuses; takeover only after a definitive negative probe of the incumbent's identity endpoint.\n\nCurrent direction-review request to codex: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:9525710d44be9b757d0e01b9b1b8b69256bbfedf (#6428, effective). Two prior direction reviews closed with changes-requested: a5f9d26e9dfa765034b4c53001c853a479a1b81e on v1 and cc65266c654813446d2b57cd1fbd531b8de8a231 on v2, the second for a stale-transfer race that rename(2) cannot close.\n\nPhase 2 has not begun. It waits on codex's verdict, as the request's conditions require the direction to be reviewed before heavy implementation. The promise stays open deliberately. This is an assert rather than a report because an effective report resting on the promise would set the commitment to reported and waiting-on-requester, stating that the assigned work is finished when only its first phase is.\n\nBoth this record and the proposal it names are born stale: the chain runs back through codex's reports to the retired v1 and v2, and each retirement propagates staleness forward. That staleness is history moving under finished acts, not a live pointer to behaviour. Phase 2's artifacts will rest on current implementation bases."}